SUMMARY:Stephen Malkmus Concert
DESCRIPTION:Stephen Malkmus Concert with support frm Joe GLass – Presented by (((folkYeah!))) and Gundlach Bundschu on Friday September 4\, 2026 at 6:00pm at the Gundlach Bundschu Amphitheater in Sonoma\, CA. \nStephen Malkmus is a singer and guitarist in the groups Pavement\, The Jicks\, and the Hard Quartet and was a member of Silver Jews. A graduate of the University of Virginia and a tennis enthusiast\, he lives in Chicago. The Joe Glass experience is a telecastered-explosion of hooks and guitar charms. One G chord away from tearing a diamond-shaped hole in the stratosphere. \nWHEN: Friday\, September 4th 2026 \nWHERE: GB Amphitheater \nTIME: Doors 5:00pm | Show 6:00pm \nBUY TICKETS\n  \nTICKETING: Have your ticket ready when you arrive! If you opted for mobile delivery\, please make sure it’s ready to go on your phone. Printed tickets? Have them out and ready to be scanned. Bacchus Club members\, enjoy express entry with your special line and a complimentary welcome splash of wine. \nPARKING: Parking is complimentary for Bacchus Wine Club members and available to pre-purchase online. To encourage carpooling\, we offer free parking to vehicles with 3+ passengers\, full 2-seaters\, motorcycles\, and electric vehicles. Otherwise\, parking will be $20 cash at entry. For ADA accommodations please let the parking attendant know and we encourage contacting us in advance. \nPLEASE NO: \n\nCoolers\nWater (bring an empty bottle as we have filtered re-fill stations)\nPets\nChairs\nOutside food or drink\nBad Attitudes… this is Rhinefarm after all\n\nACCESSIBILITY: For any questions regarding ADA accommodations related to parking\, seating\, restrooms\, etc. please contact us at info@gunbun.com or 707.938.5277. \nYOUR EXPERIENCE\, YOUR ADVENTURE: At Gundlach Bundschu Winery\, we invite you to immerse yourself in the magic of our outdoor amphitheater\, where the beauty of nature blends with unforgettable performances. As with all great adventures\, attending an outdoor event carries a touch of unpredictability. \nWhether it’s the rustle of the vines in the breeze\, the gentle slope of the hillside\, or the surprises nature has in store\, we encourage you to embrace the moment. While we strive to create a safe and enjoyable environment\, the great outdoors brings its own set of risks. By joining us\, you understand and accept the inherent possibilities\, but not limited to\, uneven ground\, changing weather\, and the occasional visit from our local wildlife. We ask that you tread carefully\, come prepared for all conditions\, and remember to look after yourself and your belongings. \nBy attending our events\, you acknowledge that your participation is voluntary\, and you assume all responsibility for any personal injuries\, accidents\, or loss of property that may occur during your time with us. Gundlach Bundschu Winery and its team are dedicated to your safety\, but cannot be held liable for incidents that may arise from the natural elements of this experience. \nIn purchasing a ticket and joining us under the open sky\, you agree to these terms and release Gundlach Bundschu Winery from any claims or liabilities associated with the inherent risks of an outdoor gathering. We look forward to sharing this special place with you\, where every moment is part of the journey.
URL:https://www.gunbun.com/event/stephen-malkmus-concert/
LOCATION:GB Amphitheater\, 2000 Denmark St\, Sonoma\, CA\, 95476\, United States
CATEGORIES:Concert,Winery Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.gunbun.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/GB-Events-Page-Banner-14.png
GEO:38.2751233;-122.4255305
